# Engineering workflow

Inspect the current code and the user's stated constraints, implement authorized work, and verify the affected contract. Ask for missing information only when it blocks a necessary step.

There is no running Synesis system. Use local tests and recorded evidence; do not inspect or restore a historical cluster as a prerequisite. Separate verification of code behavior from claims about live model quality or operating cost.

Report what changed, relevant checks and material limitations. Preserve user changes and keep private sources, credentials and generated libraries out of commits.
